     :confidence 1.0,
     :last-update "2026-09-22T10:16:07.202339-05:00"},
    :avoid-when
    ["the output doesn't have formal validation rules — use iterative-refinement instead (fixed-N polish)"
     "the validation requires deep judgment (taste, factuality) — use a tree-level judge or LLM evaluation instead"
     "the retry rate is expected to be near zero — direct :llm with :max-retries on its own retry budget is simpler"
     ":max-retries is not set OR is set above ~5 AND the producer is :llm-driven"
     "the validation rules can be expressed in code AND the validator is being implemented as another :llm node"],
    :strengths
    [{:trait
      "the validator stage being :code (not :llm) gives the loop a CORRECTNESS oracle — the producer can be creative, the validator is trusted",
      :good-when
      "the validation rules are formal/syntactic AND can be expressed in code (schema validation, regex match, parse-and-check)",
